      "id": 1,
      "text": "Settled in 1823, Dundee became an incorporated village in 1855, marking its early growth in Monroe County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundee%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dubbed the 'Hub of the Highways,' Dundee sits where M‑50 and US 23 meet, a historic crossroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundee%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The River Raisin winds through Dundee before joining Monroe and heading toward Lake Erie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundee%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Triangle Park hosts a 1913 World War I memorial bandstand, a quiet tribute amid Dundee’s historic downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
